<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<!--
  Space walking for the Shipcracker armor under Vanilla Gravship Expanded.

  Stock Odyssey marks the Space terrain Impassable. VGE1's SpaceTraversal.xml makes
  it Standable at pathCost 490 for every pawn, so the suit does not unlock space
  walking; it makes the crawl bearable. The speed knob is VEF's
  ApparelExtension.moveSpeedFactorByTerrainTag: its transpiler in
  Pawn_PathFollower.CostToMoveIntoCell divides the whole per-cell tick cost
  (the wearer's ticks per move plus the terrain's 490) by the factor, before the
  450 clamp, whenever the cell's TerrainDef.tags holds the key (Odyssey tags Space
  with "Space"). The dedicated pack is VGE2's astrorig (VGE_Apparel_Astrorig,
  factor 27.5), not a VGE1 item; the mechanism is VEF's and VGE1 alone makes it
  meaningful, which is why this patch sits in the VGE1 root and the main tree
  carries nothing.

  Factor 19: for a wearer at the 4.6 c/s baseline (13 ticks per move),
  (13 + 490) / 19 = 26.5 ticks per cell, about half walking speed in open space
  and a clear step below the astrorig's (13 + 490) / 27.5 = 18.3 (about 70
  percent). Unaided, the same cell costs the clamped 450 ticks.

  Appended to the armor's existing ApparelExtension (the one holding the trait swap
  and capacity floors). That entry carries priority 1 for a reason that decides
  whether this field exists at all: VFEP's armor base has its own ApparelExtension,
  VEF merges the two at resolve time and its Merge drops this one field, so the
  factor only survives on the entry that wins the merge. See the armor def's header.
-->
<Patch>
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationAdd">
    <xpath>Defs/VFEPirates.WarcasketDef[defName="SCWC_Warcasket_Shipcracker"]/modExtensions/li[@Class="VEF.Apparels.ApparelExtension"]</xpath>
    <value>
      <moveSpeedFactorByTerrainTag>
        <li>
          <key>Space</key>
          <value>
            <li>
              <moveSpeedFactor>19</moveSpeedFactor>
            </li>
          </value>
        </li>
      </moveSpeedFactorByTerrainTag>
    </value>
  </Operation>
</Patch>
